IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc8-part8-murder`
IMPORT `ccc8-part8-assaults`

-- ccc8-part8-harm.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART VIII: sections 244 to 248 (bodily harm and acts and omissions causing danger to the person),
-- 262 (impeding attempt to save life), 263 (duty to safeguard opening in ice, excavation on land) and 263.1 (violence against intimate partner).
-- (Sections 249 to 261 are repealed: see ccc8-repealed.l4.) It imports ccc8-part8-murder (s 236(1), manslaughter) and ccc8-part8-assaults (s 269) for the offences section 263(3) names.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING). Offences answer JUST TRUE or NOTHING (M1).
-- Answers taken from other sections enter as inputs named for them (`by s 2 firearm`, `by s 2 bodily harm`, `by s 2 criminal organization`, `by s 3.01`, `by s 2 intimate partner`).

§ `Section 244 -- Discharging firearm with intent`

-- src:4802 | 244 (1) Every person commits an offence who discharges a firearm at a person with intent to wound, maim or disfigure, to endanger the life of or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person — whether or not that person is the one at whom the firearm is discharged.
@ref s 244(1) (src:4802-4802)
GIVEN `the thing discharged is a firearm, by s 2 firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person discharges it at a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure, to endanger the life of or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(1) the person commits the offence of discharging a firearm with intent` MEANS
    IF `the thing discharged is a firearm, by s 2 firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person discharges it at a person` AND `the person does so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure, to endanger the life of or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who discharges a firearm at a person with intent to wound, maim or disfigure, to endanger the life of or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person" (marginal reading M1)

-- src:4804 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4805 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:4806 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:4807 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years; and
-- src:4808 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 244(2) (src:4804-4808)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 244(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:4806 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
@ref s 244(2)(a)(i) (src:4806-4806)
`s 244(2)(a)(i) five years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE

-- src:4807 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years; and
@ref s 244(2)(a)(ii) (src:4807-4807)
`s 244(2)(a)(ii) seven years` MEANS `Length of time` OF 7, 0, 0, FALSE

-- src:4810 | (3) In determining, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a), whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:4811 | (a) an offence under this section;
-- src:4812 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244.2; or
-- src:4813 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:4814 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref s 244(3) (src:4810-4814)
-- Fork F10 (see s 239(2)): the same ten-year rule, counted the same way.
GIVEN `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
      `the number of days spent in custody between those two days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(3) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the earlier offence is one of those listed` AND `ten years have elapsed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody"
        IF `the earlier offence is one of those listed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence"
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section`
        `the subsection` MEANS `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection`
        `the earlier offence is one of those listed` MEANS
               `the section` EQUALS 244
            OR (`the section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR `the section` EQUALS 244.2
            OR (elem `the section` (LIST 220, 236, 239, 272, 273, 279.1, 344, 346) AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`)
            OR (`the section` EQUALS 279 AND `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`)
        `ten years have elapsed` MEANS
            `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` AT LEAST (`add years` `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` 10 PLUS `the number of days spent in custody between those two days`)

-- src:4816 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction.
@ref s 244(4) (src:4816-4816)
GIVEN `the question is whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence for the purposes of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(4) the sequence of commission of offences is to be considered` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether a convicted person has committed a second or subsequent offence for the purposes of subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences or whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (3)"

-- src:4804 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:4805 | (a) if a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence or if the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:4806 | (i) in the case of a first offence, five years, and
-- src:4807 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, seven years; and
-- src:4808 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 244(2) (src:4804-4808)
GIVEN `the answers of s 244(3) for each earlier conviction of the person` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(2)(a) the offence is a first offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN earlier YIELD earlier EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of s 244(3) for each earlier conviction of the person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence" (an earlier offence is to be considered)
        IF all (GIVEN earlier YIELD earlier EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the answers of s 244(3) for each earlier conviction of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer of subsection (3) is itself not covered

@ref s 244(2) (src:4804-4808)
GIVEN `a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a first offence, by s 244(2)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 244(2) the limb that applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` OR `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `it is a first offence, by s 244(2)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 244(2)(a)(i) five years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
        IF (`a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` OR `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `it is a first offence, by s 244(2)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `s 244(2)(a)(ii) seven years`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
        IF (`a restricted firearm or prohibited firearm is used in the commission of the offence` OR `the offence is committed for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization, by s 2 criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether it is a first offence is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

@ref s 244(2) (src:4804-4808)
GIVEN `the limb that applies, by s 244(2)` IS A MAYBE Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 244(2) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limb that applies, by s 244(2)`
    WHEN JUST limb THEN LIST limb
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY   -- the limb is not covered: the empty list is the "not covered" value here (the caller sees `s 244(2) the limb that applies` answer NOTHING)

-- src:4818 | 244.1 Every person who, with intent
-- src:4819 | (a) to wound, maim or disfigure any person,
-- src:4820 | (b) to endanger the life of any person, or
-- src:4821 | (c) to prevent the arrest or detention of any person,
-- src:4822 | discharges an air or compressed gas gun or pistol at any person, whether or not that person is the person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c), is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 244.1 (src:4818-4822)
GIVEN `the thing discharged is an air or compressed gas gun or pistol` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person discharges it at any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure any person, to endanger the life of any person or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244.1 the person commits the offence of discharging an air or compressed gas gun or pistol with intent` MEANS
    IF `the thing discharged is an air or compressed gas gun or pistol` AND `the person discharges it at any person` AND `the person does so with intent to wound, maim or disfigure any person, to endanger the life of any person or to prevent the arrest or detention of any person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, with intent (a) to wound, maim or disfigure any person, (b) to endanger the life of any person, or (c) to prevent the arrest or detention of any person, discharges an air or compressed gas gun or pistol at any person ... is guilty of an indictable offence" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 244.1 (src:4818-4822)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 244.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 244.1 (src:4818-4822)
`s 244.1 the limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 244.1 (src:4818-4822)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 244.1 the punishment` MEANS LIST `s 244.1 the limb`

§ `Section 244.2 -- Discharging firearm: recklessness`

-- src:4828 | (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1)(a), place means any building or structure — or part of one — or any motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer.
@ref s 244.2(2) (src:4828-4828)
GIVEN `it is a building or structure, or part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244.2(2) place` MEANS
    IF `it is a building or structure, or part of one` OR `it is a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "place means any building or structure — or part of one — or any motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer" (for the purpose of paragraph (1)(a))

-- src:4824 | 244.2 (1) Every person commits an offence
-- src:4825 | (a) who intentionally discharges a firearm into or at a place, knowing that or being reckless as to whether another person is present in the place; or
-- src:4826 | (b) who intentionally discharges a firearm while being reckless as to the life or safety of another person.
@ref s 244.2(1) (src:4824-4826)
GIVEN `the thing discharged is a firearm, by s 2 firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person intentionally discharges it into or at a place, by s 244.2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, another person is present in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intentionally discharges it while being reckless as to the life or safety of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244.2(1) the person commits the offence of discharging a firearm recklessly` MEANS
    IF `the thing discharged is a firearm, by s 2 firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND ((`the person intentionally discharges it into or at a place, by s 244.2(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person knows that, or is reckless as to whether, another person is present in the place`) OR `the person intentionally discharges it while being reckless as to the life or safety of another person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence (a) who intentionally discharges a firearm into or at a place, knowing that or being reckless as to whether another person is present in the place; or (b) who intentionally discharges a firearm while being reckless as to the life or safety of another person" (marginal reading M1)

