-- src:4838 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2) or section 244; or
-- src:4839 | (c) an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346 if a firearm was used in the commission of the offence.
-- src:4840 | However, an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody.
@ref s 244.2(4) (src:4836-4840)
-- Fork F10 (see s 239(2)): the same ten-year rule, counted the same way.
GIVEN `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
      `the number of days spent in custody between those two days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244.2(4) the earlier conviction is to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the earlier offence is one of those listed` AND `ten years have elapsed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an earlier offence shall not be taken into account if 10 years have elapsed between the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence and the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed, not taking into account any time in custody"
        IF `the earlier offence is one of those listed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence"
    WHERE
        `the section` MEANS `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section`
        `the subsection` MEANS `the earlier offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection`
        `the earlier offence is one of those listed` MEANS
               `the section` EQUALS 244.2
            OR (`the section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR `the section` EQUALS 244
            OR (elem `the section` (LIST 220, 236, 239, 272, 273, 279.1, 344, 346) AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`)
            OR (`the section` EQUALS 279 AND `the subsection` EQUALS "(1)" AND `a firearm was used in the commission of the earlier offence`)
        `ten years have elapsed` MEANS
            `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` AT LEAST (`add years` `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` 10 PLUS `the number of days spent in custody between those two days`)

