§ `Sections 245 to 248`

-- src:4852 | (3) In subsection (2), medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner and nurse practitioner have the same meanings as in section 241.1.
@ref s 245(3) (src:4852-4852)
GIVEN `the answer of section 241.1 for the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(3) the term has the meaning it has in section 241.1` MEANS `the answer of section 241.1 for the term`   -- the same answer as section 241.1 gives for medical assistance in dying, medical practitioner or nurse practitioner

-- src:4848 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to
-- src:4849 | (a) a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2; and
-- src:4850 | (b) a person who does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2.
@ref s 245(2) (src:4848-4850)
GIVEN `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying, by s 245(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying, by s 245(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is in accordance with section 241.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(2) subsection 245(1) applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `it is in accordance with section 241.2` AND (`the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying, by s 245(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying, by s 245(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to (a) a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides medical assistance in dying in accordance with section 241.2; and (b) a person who does anything for the purpose of aiding a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner to provide medical assistance in dying"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply to"

-- src:4844 | 245 (1) Every person who administers or causes to be administered to any other person or causes any other person to take poison or any other destructive or noxious thing is guilty
-- src:4845 | (a) of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years, if they did so with intent to endanger the life of or to cause bodily harm to that person; or
-- src:4846 | (b) of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or of an offence punishable on summary conviction, if they did so with intent to aggrieve or annoy that person.
@ref s 245(1) (src:4844-4846)
DECLARE `s 245(1) intent` IS ONE OF
    `s 245(1)(a) with intent to endanger the life of or to cause bodily harm to that person`
    `s 245(1)(b) with intent to aggrieve or annoy that person`

@ref s 245(1) (src:4844-4846)
