      `the ice is open to or frequented by the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263(1) the person is under a legal duty to guard the opening in ice` MEANS
    IF `the person makes or causes to be made an opening in ice` AND `the ice is open to or frequented by the public`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who makes or causes to be made an opening in ice that is open to or frequented by the public is under a legal duty to guard it"

