-- src:4903 | 263 (1) Every one who makes or causes to be made an opening in ice that is open to or frequented by the public is under a legal duty to guard it in a manner that is adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and is adequate to warn them that the opening exists.
-- src:4904 | Excavation on land
-- src:4905 | (2) Every one who leaves an excavation on land that he owns or of which he has charge or supervision is under a legal duty to guard it in a manner that is adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and is adequate to warn them that the excavation exists.
@ref s 263(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4903-4905)
DECLARE `s 263 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 263(1) guard the opening in ice in a manner that is adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and is adequate to warn them that the opening exists`
    `s 263(2) guard the excavation in a manner that is adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and is adequate to warn them that the excavation exists`

@ref s 263(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4903-4905)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 263 act`
`s 263(1) the duty to guard the opening in ice` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 263(1) guard the opening in ice in a manner that is adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and is adequate to warn them that the opening exists`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 263(1): the opening in ice was not guarded in a manner adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and to warn them that it exists"

@ref s 263(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:4903-4905)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 263 act`
`s 263(2) the duty to guard the excavation` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `s 263(2) guard the excavation in a manner that is adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and is adequate to warn them that the excavation exists`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused` BECAUSE "s 263(2): the excavation was not guarded in a manner adequate to prevent persons from falling in by accident and to warn them that it exists"

-- src:4907 | (3) Every one who fails to perform a duty imposed by subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of
-- src:4908 | (a) manslaughter, if the death of any person results therefrom;
-- src:4909 | (b) an offence under section 269, if bodily harm to any person results therefrom; or
-- src:4910 | (c) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 263(3) (src:4907-4910)
DECLARE `s 263(3) offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter`
    `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269`
    `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 263(3) (src:4907-4910)
GIVEN `the person is under a legal duty imposed by subsection (1) or (2), by s 263(1) or (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death of any person results from the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `bodily harm to any person results from the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 263(3) offence`
`s 263(3) the offence the person commits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is under a legal duty imposed by subsection (1) or (2), by s 263(1) or (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person fails to perform the duty` AND `the death of any person results from the failure`
        THEN JUST `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter`
        IF `the person is under a legal duty imposed by subsection (1) or (2), by s 263(1) or (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person fails to perform the duty` AND `bodily harm to any person results from the failure`
        THEN JUST `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269`
        IF `the person is under a legal duty imposed by subsection (1) or (2), by s 263(1) or (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person fails to perform the duty`
        THEN JUST `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who fails to perform a duty imposed by subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of (a) manslaughter, if the death of any person results therefrom; (b) an offence under section 269, if bodily harm to any person results therefrom; or (c) an offence punishable on summary conviction" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 263(3) (src:4907-4910)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 263(3) offence`
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 263(3) the class of the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter` THEN `s 236(1) the class of the offence`
    WHEN `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269` THEN `s 269 the class of the offence`
    WHEN `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 263(3) (src:4907-4910)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 263(3) offence`
      `a firearm is used in the commission of the manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 263(3) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 263(3)(a) manslaughter` THEN `s 236(1) the punishment` `a firearm is used in the commission of the manslaughter`
    WHEN `s 263(3)(b) an offence under section 269` THEN `s 269 the punishment` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN `s 263(3)(c) an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 263.1 -- Violence against intimate partner`

-- src:4920 | (3) Everyone who is found guilty of an indictable offence under subsection (1) is liable to a term of imprisonment of not more than
-- src:4921 | (a) five years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is two years or more but less than five years;
-- src:4922 | (b) 10 years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is five years or more but less than 10 years;
-- src:4923 | (c) 14 years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is 10 years or more but less than 14 years; or
-- src:4924 | (d) life, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is 14 years or more and up to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 263.1(3) (src:4920-4924)
-- "two years less a day" is less than two years: the whole months are lowered by a hundredth of a month when `less a day` is TRUE.
GIVEN term IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 263.1(3) the months in the maximum term of imprisonment` MEANS
    (term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months) MINUS (IF term's `less a day` THEN 0.01 ELSE 0)

@ref s 263.1(3) (src:4920-4924)
GIVEN `the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE Imprisonment
`s 263.1(3) the term of imprisonment of which the person is liable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST `imprisonment for life`   -- (d) "14 years or more and up to imprisonment for life"
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `s 263.1(3) the months in the maximum term of imprisonment` term AT LEAST 168 THEN JUST `imprisonment for life`   -- (d)
            IF `s 263.1(3) the months in the maximum term of imprisonment` term AT LEAST 120 THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`)   -- (c) 10 years or more but less than 14 years
            IF `s 263.1(3) the months in the maximum term of imprisonment` term AT LEAST 60 THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (b) five years or more but less than 10 years
            IF `s 263.1(3) the months in the maximum term of imprisonment` term AT LEAST 24 THEN JUST (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)   -- (a) two years or more but less than five years
            OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) five years, if the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence is two years or more": no band below two years
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): no maximum imprisonment is stated for the included offence

-- src:4912 | 263.1 (1) Everyone who commits an offence — referred to in this section as the “included offence” — in which violence is used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner is
-- src:4913 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to the punishment provided for in subsection (3); or
-- src:4914 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 263.1(1) (src:4912-4914)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence, referred to in this section as the "included offence"` IS A BOOLEAN
      `violence is used, threatened or attempted in the included offence, by s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the violence is against their intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263.1(1) the person commits the offence of violence against an intimate partner` MEANS
    IF `the person commits an offence, referred to in this section as the "included offence"` AND `violence is used, threatened or attempted in the included offence, by s 3.01 the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the violence is against their intimate partner, by s 2 intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who commits an offence ... in which violence is used, threatened or attempted against their intimate partner is (a) guilty of an indictable offence ...; or (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 263.1(1) (src:4912-4914)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 263.1(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 263.1(1) (src:4912-4914)
GIVEN `the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence` IS AN Imprisonment
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 263.1(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 263.1(3) the term of imprisonment of which the person is liable` `the maximum term of imprisonment for the included offence`
    WHEN JUST term THEN LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, term, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3) has no band for the included offence, so only the summary limb is stated

-- src:4916 | (2) No proceedings under subsection (1) shall be
-- src:4917 | (a) commenced by way of indictment if the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings; or
-- src:4918 | (b) commenced by way of summary conviction proceedings if the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of indictment.
@ref s 263.1(2) (src:4916-4918)
GIVEN `the mode in which the proceedings are commenced` IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263.1(2) proceedings under subsection (1) may be commenced in that mode` MEANS
    IF (`the mode in which the proceedings are commenced` EQUALS `by indictment` AND `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings`) OR (`the mode in which the proceedings are commenced` EQUALS `on summary conviction` AND `the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of indictment`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings under subsection (1) shall be (a) commenced by way of indictment if the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of summary conviction proceedings; or (b) commenced by way of summary conviction proceedings if the included offence may be prosecuted only by way of indictment"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings ... shall be ... commenced ... if" (the text says only when proceedings may not be commenced)

-- src:4926 | (4) Subject to paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) and subsections (2) and (3), any provision of this Act or any other Act of Parliament — including one in respect of procedure, orders or consequences — that would have been applicable in relation to the included offence applies in relation to an offence under subsection (1).
@ref s 263.1(4) (src:4926-4926)
GIVEN `a provision of this Act or any other Act of Parliament, including one in respect of procedure, orders or consequences, would have been applicable in relation to the included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is inconsistent with paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) or subsections (2) and (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 263.1(4) the provision applies in relation to an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is inconsistent with paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) or subsections (2) and (3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) and subsections (2) and (3)"
        IF `a provision of this Act or any other Act of Parliament, including one in respect of procedure, orders or consequences, would have been applicable in relation to the included offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any provision ... that would have been applicable in relation to the included offence applies in relation to an offence under subsection (1)"
